Subject: [PATCH] Read photo and thumbnail sizes from the environment

A self-hosted install has different trade-offs from the hosted service: grid
thumbnails generated at 500 px look soft on a large or high-density screen, and
the processed original is the only copy a lightbox can show. Hard-coded sizes
leave no way to tune that without editing the source.

--- a/config/picstome.php
+++ b/config/picstome.php
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 
 return [
 
-    'photo_resize' => 2048,
+    'photo_resize' => (int) env('PICSTOME_PHOTO_RESIZE', 2048),
 
     /**
      * Fake payments mode: skips Stripe completely so the payment flow can be
@@ -11,9 +11,9 @@
     'payments_fake' => (bool) env('PAYMENTS_FAKE', false)
         && env('APP_ENV', 'production') === 'local',
 
-    'photo_thumb_resize' => 1000,
+    'photo_thumb_resize' => (int) env('PICSTOME_PHOTO_THUMB_RESIZE', 1000),
 
-    'photo_small_thumb_resize' => 500,
+    'photo_small_thumb_resize' => (int) env('PICSTOME_PHOTO_SMALL_THUMB_RESIZE', 500),
 
     /**
      * Presigned URL lifetime for individual photo downloads. Videos use a
